# finsec-ops Cursor Rules

Follow `AGENTS.md` as the authoritative repository policy. Begin with
`README.md` and `docs/index.md`, then inspect only task-relevant code, schema,
tests, documentation, and active ADRs.

finsec-ops is a Technology Financial Operations platform with cybersecurity as
the initial configured domain. Preserve the application shell, Budget worksheet
concept, Maintenance Renewals register, primary workflows, and module
boundaries. Do not expand it into ERP, accounting, GRC, ticketing, project
management, vulnerability management, asset management, or full procurement.

Use strict TypeScript. Keep business rules outside presentation components.
Preserve Server Component, server action, service, validation, DTO, and Prisma
boundaries. Use bounded server-side queries, explicit serializable DTOs,
server-side relationship validation, and transactions for multi-record
invariants. Preserve inactive references and historical financial and
operational data.

Never reset, destructively seed, or casually migrate a shared or
production-like database. Read `docs/database-and-migrations.md` before database
work. Treat authentication, authorization, binary document storage, complete
audit, and production observability as unimplemented until code proves
otherwise.

Run risk-appropriate formatting, lint, type, test, browser, build, and migration
checks. Update the authoritative topic document and material ADRs. Keep
`TODO.md` unresolved; Git history records completed work. Preserve unrelated
worktree changes and avoid unrelated refactors or broad redesign.
